From de803361731cc5ce2d411977befad53a298ae57a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CipherScope <dev@cipherscope.io>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 22:28:38 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 55/65] script: add P2MR leaf version 0xe0, whose elliptic
 curve checks can be disabled

Leaf version 0xe0 (P2MR_LEAF_TRIPWIRED, control byte 0xe1) executes in a
P2MR leaf of depth one or more as leaf version 0xc0 does, when the new
SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR_TRIPWIRE flag is set: the same tapscript rules,
validation weight budget, OP_SUCCESSx pre-scan and signature message, with
the leaf version in the tapleaf hash, and OP_CHECKMLDSA44 where
SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR_MLDSA44 is set too. Without the flag it stays an unknown
leaf version, and in P2TR it is one whatever the flags. No deployment sets
the flag yet.

The second new flag, SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR_EC_DISABLED, makes a signature
check with a 32-byte public key and a non-empty signature fail the script in
such a leaf, with the new error SCRIPT_ERR_P2MR_EC_DISABLED ("Elliptic curve
signature checks are disabled in this leaf"). The check sits in
EvalChecksigTapscript after the validation weight is charged and the public
key size is looked at, and before CheckSchnorrSignature, so neither the
signature nor the signature cache is consulted, and OP_NOT cannot turn the
outcome around. Empty signatures, empty and other-size public keys,
OP_CHECKMLDSA44, leaf version 0xc0, P2TR, legacy and witness v0 scripts are
unaffected.

ScriptExecutionData gains m_tripwired_leaf, false unless set, which only the
P2MR branch sets, for a leaf of version 0xe0 at depth one or more with
SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR_TRIPWIRE. The two flag names are P2MR_TRIPWIRE and
P2MR_EC_DISABLED.

The script_flags fuzz target, whose check is that removing flags from a
pass or adding flags to a failure keeps the result, no longer adds or
removes SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR, SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR_MLDSA44 and
SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR_TRIPWIRE: each turns a script that a DISCOURAGE flag
refuses into one that executes, so either change can turn the result
around. The first two came with earlier patches and break the check in
the same way. SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR_EC_DISABLED only makes more scripts fail,
and is fuzzed.

See doc/p2mr-tripwire.md, added later in this series.
